WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.520
Long ago, an everlasting being called the Sakura Dragon took root in Ashina's lands

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:08.399
From it, flowed various forms of immortality

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:11.910
Powers that would go on to corrupt the lives of men

00:00:12.309 --> 00:00:14.901
One of these was the Dragon's heritage,

00:00:14.901 --> 00:00:17.759
A direct line to the dragons undying blood.

00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:20.513
And from that blood came the rejuvenating waters

00:00:20.600 --> 00:00:24.600
Which was a bewitching force that grants great resilience to one's flesh

00:00:25.040 --> 00:00:32.660
However, this power was never meant for Japan and from these gifts stemmed infestations and rot

00:00:33.060 --> 00:00:40.260
Leading many, like Kuro, a divine heir, to ponder whether this power was a blessing or a curse.

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:45.360
So, atop Ashina castle, our goal becomes to sever this immortality and

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:48.840
what better weapon for this task than the crimson mortal blade?

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:53.867
This is one of two weapons in this world that's capable of wounding immortal beings

00:00:53.867 --> 00:00:56.820
And once we ascend to the dragon's realm with this sword

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:58.800
We can rebuke its power

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:03.720
The crimson mortal blades true name, after all, is the Gracious Gift of Tears

00:01:04.120 --> 00:01:09.160
And, by making the dragon cry, we reject its gift of everlasting life.

00:01:09.720 --> 00:01:11.380
Sekiro: "Where is this mortal blade?"

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:14.180
Isshin Ashina: "I've heard it's held in the Senpou Temple.

00:01:14.180 --> 00:01:17.160
The gates to that temple are closed now, though.

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:21.920
Who knows what those degenerates are doing, shut away up there in the mountains."

00:01:22.080 --> 00:01:25.808
Senpou temple was once a place dedicated to Buddhist teachings.

00:01:25.808 --> 00:01:29.740
These were teachings of selflessness, of death, and of rebirth.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:30.600
However,

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:35.540
Divine Child: "Those of the Senpou temple have strayed from Buddhist teachings.

00:01:36.460 --> 00:01:38.680
They have abandoned their faith,

00:01:39.380 --> 00:01:41.700
Seduced by a search for immortality."

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:45.600
And since you are now considered an immortal being

00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:50.120
Divine Child: "Should you be captured there is no telling what would become of you,

00:01:50.540 --> 00:01:53.800
you would do well to return the way you came."

00:01:54.420 --> 00:01:58.700
Despite being these rotting degenerates infested with immortal centipedes

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:04.000
The monks may not be as evil as they're being portrayed, but we'll get to that later

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:08.380
The first monks you fight bite down on sugars to enhance their strength

00:02:08.580 --> 00:02:11.420
Which should be a strategy that's very familiar to you

00:02:11.420 --> 00:02:15.640
If you've been using these sugars that you find scattered across all of Ashina

00:02:16.020 --> 00:02:19.854
And their  placement around the world is actually very intentional

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:23.200
For, in an effort, to curry favor with the Ashina

00:02:23.280 --> 00:02:27.080
Senpou monks effectively bribed the Ashina with candy

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:33.380
They spread these sugars across all of these lands in honor of Ashina's military heroes

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:40.720
Gokan, and even Ako, Ungo, or Yashariku are statued as we first enter Senpou

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:44.940
These men once fought for their country, but they all became corrupted.

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:48.640
Turning into the headless monsters that you find throughout your travels

00:02:48.680 --> 00:02:55.500
Ungo, for example, lost his mind in defense of the state and he was beheaded, sinking to the bottom of a  moat

00:02:55.780 --> 00:03:00.920
And since these sugar blessings are coming from such tormented creatures

00:03:00.920 --> 00:03:07.960
You kind of have to wonder at what cost to us, or them, are these blessings being imparted?

00:03:08.600 --> 00:03:13.720
And, you know, while we never really do get a chance to explore Senpou temple's "candy" factory

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:17.260
The monks themselves use these sugars really liberally

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:20.860
They use every single one of them except Yashariku actually,

00:03:21.440 --> 00:03:26.360
this candy in particular puts you closer to death which made it forbidden to the monks of the temple

00:03:26.459 --> 00:03:33.619
Yet, they had no problem distributing it far and wide in the name of donations towards their costly undying research

00:03:34.020 --> 00:03:38.420
So these sugars brought them wealth and they brought them favor with the Ashina

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:45.960
And this focus on wealth in particular actually aligns with another tool of theirs, The Golden Vortex

00:03:46.080 --> 00:03:51.320
It's an upgraded version of their large fan, which forces enemies to drop items and money

00:03:51.320 --> 00:03:53.840
which are to be considered donations

00:03:54.380 --> 00:03:56.080
And it's all ironic really

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:58.160
Considering the words of their founder,

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:07.860
These are the words of the high priest and they were ideals that were upheld

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:10.640
With the tenacious mastery of martial arts

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:14.325
These martial arts culminated in the Senpou esoteric texts

00:04:14.325 --> 00:04:19.100
A tome that contains skills that are both martial arts and prayers

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:23.140
Weighted strikes that purge the self of worldly desire for

00:04:23.480 --> 00:04:30.819
Without strength, one cannot defeat the enemies of Buddha and as we know there's at least one undying enemy of Buddha

00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:33.520
Occupying a Buddhist temple in-game.

00:04:33.680 --> 00:04:37.200
Eventually, however, this ideology decayed and festered

00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:44.880
For the Senpou temple was seized by an obsession with undeath and their martial arts that were once used for virtue

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:48.820
Became used in the pursuit of immortality instead

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:54.980
There's even a curious statue sitting before their esoteric text that is consumed by flame

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:58.869
It's left half blackened and burned and if you finish the game

00:04:58.869 --> 00:05:05.340
You'll know that this could be a sign of Shura a demon that appears in the bodies of those who have lost all virtue

00:05:05.380 --> 00:05:10.620
This is a Myoo statue and these statues represented guardians of buddhist law

00:05:10.940 --> 00:05:14.280
So it being so badly damaged is wholly

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:19.020
representative of the degradation of Senpou's brand of Buddhism.

00:05:19.020 --> 00:05:22.200
This fall from grace has a lot to do with

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:25.960
Senpou's experimentation with the rejuvenating waters

00:05:26.210 --> 00:05:30.729
which, as we mentioned earlier, is a legendary source of immortality and

00:05:31.010 --> 00:05:38.559
it flows from the dragon's blood. We talked about Isshin in the last video on the first half of Sekiro that you watched and

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:43.380
He was a legendary figure who established Ashina as the dominant force in the land

00:05:43.540 --> 00:05:51.660
we spoke of how he hates the rats from the interior ministry who are preparing to invade his land but curiously

00:05:51.760 --> 00:05:58.880
He also considers these short assassins to be rats, as they spy on behalf of Senpou Temple.

00:05:59.380 --> 00:06:02.540
Soldiers of Ashina: "It seems Isshin's illness is indeed grave."

00:06:04.200 --> 00:06:06.140
"The land of Ashina will not last much longer"

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:08.660
"Even with Genichiro on our side"

00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:15.119
Here the Senpou assassins spy on Isshin, ruminating on how the land of the Ashina is doomed

00:06:15.480 --> 00:06:17.800
even with Genichiro on their side

00:06:18.120 --> 00:06:22.540
Senpou is part of Ashina after all and its monks are

00:06:23.080 --> 00:06:26.490
Equally screwed if the interior ministry invades them all

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:33.680
Especially since the interior ministry actually fears the Waters of Rejuvenation and Senpou temple has been experimenting

00:06:33.680 --> 00:06:40.280
Successfully with the Waters of Rejuvenation for years. They have a lot to lose if Ashina goes down

00:06:40.900 --> 00:06:42.989
talking more about these short assassins

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:49.440
They were originally hired to guard Senpou temple but inevitably, they became an extension

00:06:49.440 --> 00:06:55.220
of the monks will in their quest for undeath. Their mission became to kidnap children

00:06:55.220 --> 00:06:59.860
So that the Senpou monks could experiment on them with the Waters of rejuvenation.

00:06:59.860 --> 00:07:06.960
So circling back around to Isshin. It's no wonder that he considers these assassins to be rats and degenerates

00:07:06.960 --> 00:07:11.609
in fact knowledge of these experiments on children could explain why Isshin

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:17.560
Supports our quest to sever Kuro's immortality and why he's so disappointed

00:07:17.580 --> 00:07:24.500
in Genichiro's use of the rejuvenating waters since his grandson Genichiro actually sided with the

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:30.380
degenerates of Senpou. In fact, there's evidence to suggest that Genichiro was actually

00:07:30.380 --> 00:07:36.600
Encouraging even more research on the rejuvenating waters through Dosaku who you would have seen

00:07:36.820 --> 00:07:40.520
Experimenting with them on Ashina's behalf in the abandoned dungeon

00:07:41.220 --> 00:07:46.280
This place is right outside of Senpou temple and Dosaku wears a garb. That's actually

00:07:46.540 --> 00:07:51.719
Identical to that of the bomb-thrower monks, in addition he fights with their martial arts

00:07:52.020 --> 00:07:54.980
cementing the connection between the two places and

00:07:55.420 --> 00:08:00.240
Considering this man was an ex disciple of Dogen who is another important character

00:08:00.240 --> 00:08:06.769
I wouldn't be surprised if Dogen was also involved with experiments on the rejuvenating children as well

00:08:07.559 --> 00:08:14.928
Dotting the hills of Mt. Kongo are hundreds of little statues that are accompanied by red and white pinwheels

00:08:15.389 --> 00:08:22.729
these were offered in fond remembrance for the children that the monks sacrificed in their experiments with immortality and

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:25.580
At least one of these children is likely named

00:08:25.760 --> 00:08:29.340
Armored Warrior: "Robertttt"

00:08:29.460 --> 00:08:37.740
You might have heard of him round and round all their little pinwheels spin and yet the children are still right here

00:08:37.740 --> 00:08:45.320
Kotaro: "The spinning, spinning red and white flowers. Only one pure, white flower."

00:08:45.320 --> 00:08:49.400
And of all the children only one child survived the ritual

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:53.000
Battlefield Memorial Mob: "It was by a hair's breadth, but mercifully

00:08:53.620 --> 00:08:56.680
She survived. Oh, she must have suffered greatly

00:08:57.260 --> 00:08:58.680
you'd best treat her kindly."

00:08:59.200 --> 00:09:04.280
This member of the Memorial mob still remembers the event and it makes sense, right?

00:09:04.280 --> 00:09:10.460
Because where you find the departed, you will find the memorial mob .Curiously though, when he

00:09:10.460 --> 00:09:16.600
Contracts dragon rot. He actually draws a parallel to what the children went through during the experiment

00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:19.890
Battlefield Memorial Mob: "Divine children, forgive me."

00:09:19.890 --> 00:09:20.900
Sekiro: "What's wrong with you?"

00:09:21.600 --> 00:09:24.500
Battlefield Memorial Mob: "Buddha's Just in righteous punishment.

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:29.960
I had no idea the divine children were suffering so badly.

00:09:30.680 --> 00:09:33.640
I see now. I must make an offering."

00:09:34.280 --> 00:09:35.120
He feels guilty

00:09:35.740 --> 00:09:40.380
But none should feel more guilt than those who are directly responsible

00:09:41.260 --> 00:09:45.760
Master of the Senpou Temple: "Children of the rejuvenating waters.

00:09:46.620 --> 00:09:50.960
Forgive me, that child

00:09:51.260 --> 00:09:56.880
She's the only one left. She must be lonely

00:09:57.600 --> 00:10:01.640
Trapped in that room by herself...

00:10:03.120 --> 00:10:08.620
So you're the one who works for the divine heir of the Dragon's Blood?"

00:10:08.740 --> 00:10:10.180
Sekiro: "That's right."

00:10:10.180 --> 00:10:19.380
Master of Senpou Temple: "The divine heir is truly exalted, but exalted or not, man is still man.

00:10:21.060 --> 00:10:26.700
I'm so foolish that I didn't understand that myself.

00:10:27.800 --> 00:10:33.060
Don't, don't leave your divine heir on his own.

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:37.920
Leave! It's too late to regret once you've already lost them."

00:10:38.560 --> 00:10:45.269
This man is a high-ranking priest as he claims to be at fault for the divine child's confinement

00:10:45.960 --> 00:10:51.500
Furthermore, he's proof that the monks knew that their experiment was successful

00:10:51.540 --> 00:10:58.060
But, ironically, it also seems like it's impossible for them to reach the realm where she resides

00:10:58.440 --> 00:11:00.440
Master of Senpou Temple: "It's my fault,

00:11:00.560 --> 00:11:02.520
the child,

00:11:02.520 --> 00:11:06.840
She's confined within the inner sanctum.

00:11:06.840 --> 00:11:09.540
It's impossible to see her now."

00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:14.969
Why? Well, this is just speculation. But my theory is that Buddha himself

00:11:15.850 --> 00:11:23.100
Protects the realm where the divine child resides because this space that she's at lies past the illusory halls

00:11:23.500 --> 00:11:27.209
This is a realm protected by the folding screen monkeys

00:11:27.550 --> 00:11:31.649
Beings that are said to occupy a space between life and death

00:11:32.200 --> 00:11:38.900
These guys are a play on a proverb that you've probably heard- see no evil, hear no evil, speak no evil.

00:11:38.900 --> 00:11:42.120
This is a famous proverb of Buddhist tradition

00:11:42.120 --> 00:11:47.780
And there's even an invisible fourth monkey who was a reference to the 'do no evil'

00:11:47.780 --> 00:11:52.680
Principle then they often leave out when they're talking about this legend. This to me

00:11:53.009 --> 00:11:59.129
Is evidence that the Senpou monks turned a blind eye, a deaf ear, a mute voice

00:11:59.350 --> 00:12:05.130
Upon their sinful path to enlightenment and it's likely to me that this bossfight

00:12:05.740 --> 00:12:07.660
represents that fact

00:12:07.660 --> 00:12:10.199
There exists a prosthetic in Sekiro

00:12:10.329 --> 00:12:14.459
Called the large fan which allows you to spirit people away

00:12:14.459 --> 00:12:20.669
All of the monks of Senpou temple were actually spirited away once before, that's why they're here

00:12:20.920 --> 00:12:22.920
But if you spirit them away again

00:12:23.410 --> 00:12:25.529
Rumors say they'll disappear forever

00:12:26.259 --> 00:12:27.309
Unless of course,

00:12:27.309 --> 00:12:34.679
they're Kotaro, a kind Senpou monk or unless they're the other monk here in the Illusory Halls, who seems

00:12:35.050 --> 00:12:39.240
legitimately set on achieving nirvana. The fact that these two

00:12:39.850 --> 00:12:46.800
Wholesome, legitimate monks are the only beings that were actually able to reach these halls when they're spirited away twice

00:12:47.139 --> 00:12:49.589
plays into my belief that Buddha is perhaps

00:12:50.259 --> 00:12:52.800
Protecting this realm from the infested.

00:12:52.800 --> 00:12:57.359
Illusory Hall Monk: "By the way, there was once someone who, like you,

00:12:58.120 --> 00:13:03.419
was on a mission. I believe he chased the monkeys for a while, but

00:13:04.809 --> 00:13:09.420
Everything here eventually went silent."

00:13:09.420 --> 00:13:11.099
This someone is almost certainly Genichiro,

00:13:11.410 --> 00:13:16.980
he's a man with friendly links to Senpou temple, a man who is looking for the mortal blade and

00:13:17.350 --> 00:13:24.509
He's someone who would have found it impossible to catch the monkeys since he doesn't have the same talents that we have

00:13:24.699 --> 00:13:28.049
It's almost as if this was meant to be solved by us

00:13:31.630 --> 00:13:33.900
Divine Child: "Please forgive them

00:13:37.860 --> 00:13:41.120
They only sought to keep me hidden

00:13:45.700 --> 00:13:48.400
However, it seems it was not meant to be

00:13:52.060 --> 00:13:54.060
Close your eyes

00:13:56.380 --> 00:13:58.880
Let us meet at the Inner Sanctum."

00:14:00.240 --> 00:14:06.140
Here, the Divine Child of the Rejuvenating Waters parts you finally with the Mortal Blade.

00:14:06.340 --> 00:14:09.930
Which you're able to draw thanks to your resurrective powers.

00:14:12.610 --> 00:14:14.230
Sekiro: "I accept it's power."

00:14:14.230 --> 00:14:15.760
Kuro: "Wolf...

00:14:15.760 --> 00:14:17.850
That sword on your back

00:14:18.460 --> 00:14:22.520
Is it the sword that can kill those who cannot die?"

00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:23.860
Sekiro: "Yes.

00:14:23.860 --> 00:14:29.591
It was given to me by the Divine Child of the Rejuvenating Waters at Senpou Temple."

00:14:29.600 --> 00:14:32.440
Kuro: "The Divine Child of the Rejuvenating Waters?"

00:14:32.440 --> 00:14:37.860
Sekiro: "The monks at Senpou Temple abandoned the ways of their faith in pursuit of immortality,

00:14:37.860 --> 00:14:45.280
the result is those who have false dragon's heritage known as the divine children of the Rejuvenating Waters."

00:14:45.670 --> 00:14:47.670
Kuro: " A false dragon's heritage...

00:14:49.000 --> 00:14:51.000
I never would have thought... wait

00:14:51.700 --> 00:14:53.440
divine children?"

00:14:53.440 --> 00:14:58.019
Sekiro: "Yes. Many were created but only one survived."

00:14:58.440 --> 00:15:05.340
Kuro: "Further proof of the corruption this power brings to man, the ties of immortality must be severed."

00:15:05.340 --> 00:15:06.780
Sekiro: "Yes my lord."

00:15:07.030 --> 00:15:09.780
Now that you have the gracious gift of Tears

00:15:09.940 --> 00:15:15.299
We can actually acquire the Dragon's tears and sever immortality. Interestingly, though

00:15:15.400 --> 00:15:21.749
We are not the first to seek the Crimson mortal blade with immortal severance in mind many years ago

00:15:21.750 --> 00:15:26.640
There was a woman named Tomoe and a divine heir named Takeru

00:15:26.820 --> 00:15:30.320
Who tried to do the same. Tomoe's note reads

00:15:38.260 --> 00:15:39.280
what she's describing

00:15:39.280 --> 00:15:46.020
is the purification ending, where the oathbound commits sudoku (very funny) restoring the divine heir's mortality

00:15:46.440 --> 00:15:48.960
and the humanity. She goes on to write

00:16:02.980 --> 00:16:08.300
The high priest is central to everything in Senpou. He was the founder of this temple

00:16:08.610 --> 00:16:11.930
So we need to figure out what his motivations were

00:16:12.200 --> 00:16:18.840
For creating the divine child, for starting this temple, for hiding away the Mortal Blade and for creating

00:16:18.840 --> 00:16:26.060
the divine children. We find him dressed all in blue, his corpse sequestered away in a cave

00:16:26.220 --> 00:16:28.279
and instead of immortal severance

00:16:28.279 --> 00:16:32.599
Which Tomoe wanted, the high priest wanted a different ending.

00:16:32.820 --> 00:16:39.949
Turns out he was actually gunning for the Dragon's return ending which he must have looked up on a wiki or something because that shit's

00:16:40.079 --> 00:16:47.569
Complicated, but to this end and for this dragon's return ending he outlined his journey in two sacred

00:16:47.880 --> 00:16:53.359
Scriptures. The first text that describes his journey is Holy Chapter: Infested.

00:16:53.699 --> 00:16:55.699
Depending on when you arrive here,

00:16:55.730 --> 00:17:00.139
it's either in the hands of the regretful monk outside the Halls of Illusion or

00:17:00.329 --> 00:17:06.349
It's thrown to the bottom of the lake in disgust. It lays out a founding principle for Senpou temple

00:17:06.540 --> 00:17:09.700
That their journey is to spend an eternity

00:17:09.740 --> 00:17:11.860
Musing on why they cannot die

00:17:11.940 --> 00:17:17.120
The text is from the perspective of the High Priest and it reads:

00:17:34.760 --> 00:17:37.120
This text reveals a

00:17:37.120 --> 00:17:43.400
potentially major twist in Senpou Temple's law. It reveals that their founding principle isn't

00:17:43.580 --> 00:17:45.900
necessarily to acquire immortality

00:17:46.040 --> 00:17:51.420
After all the monks already assumed they were immortal from the centipedes.

00:17:51.420 --> 00:17:59.500
No, Instead their founding goal was to understand their infestation, something the high priest considered enlightenment.

00:17:59.500 --> 00:18:05.240
Although, whether it is enlightenment and whether the path to that enlightenment was justified

00:18:05.370 --> 00:18:06.809
That is another story

00:18:06.809 --> 00:18:14.389
But he believed that the Avenue to this enlightenment was the creation of a divine child of the Rejuvenating Waters

00:18:15.200 --> 00:18:20.450
and they abandoned all virtue and ethics while chasing that creation,

00:18:20.880 --> 00:18:26.599
and when you give the divine child this text it explains to her why she was created

00:18:26.600 --> 00:18:28.740
Sekiro: "I was told to give this to you."

00:18:28.740 --> 00:18:31.560
Divine Child: "Thank you. I will accept it..."

00:18:34.220 --> 00:18:35.300
Sekiro: "What's wrong?"

00:18:35.600 --> 00:18:40.062
Divine Child: "I, I still cannot help but detest them."

00:18:40.062 --> 00:18:41.360
In the end though

00:18:41.370 --> 00:18:46.069
The information within does set her on a path to the dragon's return

00:18:46.260 --> 00:18:53.180
Divine Child: There is something I would like to discuss. I believe we should aim not to sever the dragon's heritage

00:18:54.360 --> 00:18:57.880
But instead to return it to its rightful place."

00:18:58.200 --> 00:19:00.020
Sekiro: "Return the dragon's blood?"

00:19:00.020 --> 00:19:01.080
Divine Child: "That's right.

00:19:01.080 --> 00:19:07.880
The dragon's heritage was set free from its homeland and it drifted here to Japan

00:19:07.880 --> 00:19:10.340
Its power was never meant for this land

00:19:10.920 --> 00:19:12.880
Until something is done

00:19:13.560 --> 00:19:20.200
it will continue to corrupt the lives of those who encounter it, the dragon's heritage and those

00:19:20.460 --> 00:19:21.920
Connected to it.

00:19:21.929 --> 00:19:24.709
It is only right that they return home

00:19:25.289 --> 00:19:26.700
to the west

00:19:26.700 --> 00:19:29.029
to the birthplace of the divine dragon

00:19:29.600 --> 00:19:35.400
However, there is one problem. I am unsure of the exact destination."

00:19:35.820 --> 00:19:36.760
Sekiro: "Who would know?

00:19:36.760 --> 00:19:40.020
Divine Child: "Perhaps the high priest of Senpou Temple."

00:19:40.020 --> 00:19:41.000
Sekiro: "And he is?"

00:19:41.360 --> 00:19:43.680
Divine Child: "He's the founder of Senpou Temple.

00:19:44.280 --> 00:19:51.020
I wonder how old he actually is. He has secluded himself in a five-story pagoda

00:19:51.380 --> 00:19:54.440
Past the narrow cave not far from here...

00:19:55.100 --> 00:19:57.300
Shinobi of the Divine heir."

00:19:57.300 --> 00:19:58.000
Sekiro: "Yes?"

00:19:58.380 --> 00:20:01.880
Divine Child: "This path differs from that of the one to sever

00:20:01.880 --> 00:20:09.880
Immortality. I do not wish to force my opinion upon you. Should you wish to return the dragon's heritage

00:20:10.740 --> 00:20:14.480
Then prehaps you should seek out the High Senpou Priest."

00:20:14.940 --> 00:20:21.700
The infested chapter speaks of his undying journey towards understanding why he cannot die. And the second chapter :

00:20:21.880 --> 00:20:25.800
"Dragon's return" lays out his conclusions. it reads :

00:20:44.340 --> 00:20:50.180
The serpentine fruits mentioned, are the dried and fresh hearts of the Serpent's of the sunken Valley

00:20:50.860 --> 00:20:58.020
And Senpou actually has a lot of pre-existing links with the snakes and with the valley that are really easy to miss

00:20:58.330 --> 00:20:59.110
however,

00:20:59.110 --> 00:21:01.000
discussions surrounding the snakes will

00:21:01.000 --> 00:21:05.429
Continue in the 'sunken Valley' episode and will go deeper into the Dragon's return

00:21:05.429 --> 00:21:12.179
I think in the endings video. Remember to subscribe and ring the notification bell so you don't miss out by the way

00:21:12.179 --> 00:21:19.739
It's coming soon. I want to leave you on a really important topic, the infested, the centipedes. You probably thought I'd mentioned them earlier

00:21:20.350 --> 00:21:27.419
They're so core to Senpou Temple and yet I mentioned them last because just like the monks and their motivation,

00:21:27.520 --> 00:21:33.539
We don't really have enough information on them yet, in my opinion, to draw guaranteed conclusions.

00:21:33.820 --> 00:21:40.110
what we do know is that the centipedes are found within Hanbei, the Senpou monks, the guardian ape and the

00:21:40.299 --> 00:21:46.979
Corrupted monk and in all of these examples the hosts actually have a pretty symbiotic relationship with the centipede

00:21:47.230 --> 00:21:52.620
They're able to carry on their goals while infested whether it be defending a bridge

00:21:53.169 --> 00:21:54.760
meditating on undeath or

00:21:54.760 --> 00:21:57.239
Just cultivating a flower to give to a mate

00:21:57.240 --> 00:22:03.449
The centipede is more than happy to stay in the body for a ridiculous amount of time. And that might be their goal

00:22:03.450 --> 00:22:05.450
we'll get to that later but

00:22:05.590 --> 00:22:10.020
Assuming that the rejuvenating waters and the fountainhead waters are the same thing

00:22:10.210 --> 00:22:17.100
then these waters are actually what all the infested have in common the guardian ape resides in a valley where the fountain

00:22:17.380 --> 00:22:21.389
headwaters pool deeply the corrupted monk guards the fountainhead palace

00:22:21.650 --> 00:22:27.680
And could also have linked the Senpou monks who themselves have studied the waters for an age. To me

00:22:27.720 --> 00:22:32.240
It makes a lot of sense that the centipedes come from these waters after all,

00:22:32.310 --> 00:22:36.739
the waters stem from the Dragons heritage and the Dragons heritage, too

00:22:36.810 --> 00:22:40.279
Has its own form of stagnation in the form of dragon rot

00:22:40.280 --> 00:22:46.940
Which eats away at one's lifeforce the centipedes mirror that stagnation in the waters of rejuvenation

00:22:48.060 --> 00:22:52.580
Sealing it for me is that there is actually one more place that the centipedes appear

00:22:52.710 --> 00:22:56.029
It's very hard to find but deep below Fountainhead lake

00:22:56.400 --> 00:23:01.040
Surrounding the corpse of a giant carp are tens of luminescent centipedes

00:23:01.140 --> 00:23:05.780
Which might mean that they infest the very source of the rejuvenating waters

00:23:06.420 --> 00:23:07.500
interestingly

00:23:07.500 --> 00:23:13.160
giant carp in Sekiro are supposedly everlasting and have goals of becoming a dragon and

00:23:13.770 --> 00:23:18.530
the fact that some centipedes have stripped away an immortal corpse is

00:23:19.200 --> 00:23:25.879
Curious to say the least. In addition, there are multiple Japanese legends that link centipedes and Dragons

00:23:26.250 --> 00:23:32.270
But those are tales for another time for all their mentions about centipedes making the infested

00:23:32.670 --> 00:23:38.029
Immortal, they might actually not for, in the cave by the five-tier pagoda,

00:23:38.190 --> 00:23:41.119
we find the high priest and his peers as

00:23:41.370 --> 00:23:48.170
still and as dead as the centipedes that rest upon them. The nature of the High Priest's undeath is

00:23:48.360 --> 00:23:54.410
By far the most intriguing part of Senpou temple. Did he know when he was going to die?

00:23:54.440 --> 00:23:57.919
Is this why he and his peers hid away in a cave

00:23:57.920 --> 00:24:02.599
So no one would find out? Did the centipede leave their bodies once it was fully grown?

00:24:02.600 --> 00:24:07.160
Does it have some objective beyond this place? Where did it go? And

00:24:07.860 --> 00:24:15.770
also, how did this guy discover so much about the Dragon's return and what was his relationship like with the

00:24:15.770 --> 00:24:23.030
Divine child? She knows about him somehow after all. There's a lot of questions that I could speculate on for hours

00:24:23.030 --> 00:24:27.410
But this has gone too long already. I'm curious though, as always. What do you think?

00:24:27.440 --> 00:24:33.960
I've actually decided to split the majority of Sekiro's story into four parts now and I'm doing this for a few reasons

00:24:34.600 --> 00:24:39.600
partly because it allows me to go into way more detail as you can probably tell from this episode and

00:24:40.040 --> 00:24:44.529
Partly because, hey I get to Commission a bunch of incredible art for every single episode

